From: idkjashan <jashanpreetsinghbrar01@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 10:20:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] gz_bridge: report ESC output function and current

esc_status from the gz ESC interface had no actuator_function and no current,
so the failure detector skipped every ESC and 'failure motor off' had no
effect in SITL. Fill both in (current is a simple speed^2 stand-in).
---
 .../simulation/gz_bridge/GZMixingInterfaceESC.cpp        | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/modules/simulation/gz_bridge/GZMixingInterfaceESC.cpp b/src/modules/simulation/gz_bridge/GZMixingInterfaceESC.cpp
index f556817ea9..b11080d301 100644
--- a/src/modules/simulation/gz_bridge/GZMixingInterfaceESC.cpp
+++ b/src/modules/simulation/gz_bridge/GZMixingInterfaceESC.cpp
@@ -116,6 +116,15 @@ void GZMixingInterfaceESC::motorSpeedCallback(const gz::msgs::Actuators &actuato
 		esc_status.esc[i].esc_rpm = actuators.velocity(i);
 		esc_status.esc_online_flags |= 1 << i;
 
+		// Fill in the two fields the motor failure detector (FD_ACT_EN) and the failure
+		// injection key on: which motor this ESC drives, and a current. Without them every
+		// ESC maps to an invalid motor index and is skipped, so 'failure motor off' does
+		// nothing in SITL. The current is only a plausible stand-in (~speed^2, 30 A at
+		// full speed), not a motor model.
+		esc_status.esc[i].actuator_function = static_cast<uint8_t>(_mixing_output.outputFunction(i));
+		const float speed_ratio = static_cast<float>(actuators.velocity(i)) / fmaxf(_mixing_output.maxValue(i), 1.f);
+		esc_status.esc[i].esc_current = 30.f * speed_ratio * speed_ratio;
+
 		if (actuators.velocity(i) > 0) {
 			esc_status.esc_armed_flags |= 1 << i;
 		}
